// A recipe. This page is its source: edit it here.
page RecipeDarkModeSwitch(path: "/recipes/dark-mode-switch", title: "Add a dark-mode switch — Recipes", description: "Let the reader pick light, dark or the system's choice with setTheme, and mark the current choice by reading theme.") {
    RecipeShell("Add a dark-mode switch", summary: "Let the reader pick a light look, a dark one, or whatever their system prefers, and keep that choice across visits. The switch needs a dark theme named in `webfluent.app.json`:", outputs: ["website", "app", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Add a picture, sized for every screen", to: "/recipes/add-a-picture"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Add video and audio", to: "/recipes/video-and-audio"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Show an icon", to: "/recipes/show-an-icon")], source: "site/src/pages/recipes/RecipeDarkModeSwitch.wf", how: true, hasVariations: true, project: { "src/pages/DarkModeSwitch.wf": #"/// The look by day. Every token not named here keeps its baseline value.
theme Day {
    color-primary: #2563EB
    color-on-primary: #FFFFFF
    color-background: #F8FAFC
    color-surface: #FFFFFF
    color-text: #0F172A
    color-text-muted: #64748B
    color-border: #E2E8F0
}

/// The same tokens after dark.
theme Night {
    color-primary: #60A5FA
    color-on-primary: #0B1120
    color-background: #0B1120
    color-surface: #131C2E
    color-text: #E2E8F0
    color-text-muted: #94A3B8
    color-border: #1E293B
}

page Settings(path: "/settings", title: "Settings", description: "How the site looks.") {
    Heading("Settings").h1
    Row(gap: .sm) {
        Button("Light", outlined: theme != "light") { on click { setTheme("light") } }
        Button("Dark", outlined: theme != "dark") { on click { setTheme("dark") } }
        Button("Match the system", outlined: theme != "system") { on click { setTheme("system") } }
    }
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "dark-mode-switch",
  "theme": {
    "name": "Day",
    "dark": "Night"
  }
}
"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** the `theme` setting below in `webfluent.app.json`. The `spa` starter already has it, declares these two themes in `src/theme.wf`, and places a `DarkModeSwitch` component in its header (its `Night` names no `color-on-primary`; add the line below). This page replaces the starter's `src/pages/Settings.wf`. In a new project, put the themes in `src/theme.wf`.")
            DocsCodeBlock(#"{ "theme": { "name": "Day", "dark": "Night" } }"#, title: "json")
            Markdown("This program declares both themes and a settings page with three buttons, the current choice drawn solid and the others outlined:")
            DocsCodeBlock(#"/// The look by day. Every token not named here keeps its baseline value.
theme Day {
    color-primary: #2563EB
    color-on-primary: #FFFFFF
    color-background: #F8FAFC
    color-surface: #FFFFFF
    color-text: #0F172A
    color-text-muted: #64748B
    color-border: #E2E8F0
}

/// The same tokens after dark.
theme Night {
    color-primary: #60A5FA
    color-on-primary: #0B1120
    color-background: #0B1120
    color-surface: #131C2E
    color-text: #E2E8F0
    color-text-muted: #94A3B8
    color-border: #1E293B
}

page Settings(path: "/settings", title: "Settings", description: "How the site looks.") {
    Heading("Settings").h1
    Row(gap: .sm) {
        Button("Light", outlined: theme != "light") { on click { setTheme("light") } }
        Button("Dark", outlined: theme != "dark") { on click { setTheme("dark") } }
        Button("Match the system", outlined: theme != "system") { on click { setTheme("system") } }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        variations {
            Heading("One button", id: "one-button").h3

            Markdown("The built-in `ThemeToggle` is a single button that switches between the two: a moon on a light page, a sun on a dark one, named for the theme it switches to. Put it in a header:")

            DocsCodeBlock(#"app {
    Navbar {
        Navbar.Brand { Text("Ledger").bold }
        Navbar.Actions { ThemeToggle }
    }
    Router
}"#, title: "wf")

            Heading("A labelled switch", id: "a-labelled-switch").h3

            Markdown("The `spa` starter's `DarkModeSwitch` (`src/components/DarkModeSwitch.wf`) is a `Switch` labelled \"Dark mode\". It is on when the reader chose dark, or chose nothing and their system prefers dark, and it calls `setTheme` with the other one when it is flipped.")

        }
        Markdown("- **Two themes.** The config's `theme.name` is the one the site starts with and `theme.dark` the one for the dark ([Styling](/learn/13-styling#dark-mode)). A token the dark theme leaves out keeps the light theme's value, so name the same tokens in both.\n- **Every built-in draws from these tokens**, so the buttons, the cards and the fields change with the theme and nothing else needs a dark rule. A raw colour in a `style \{ \}` block does not change; use a token there (`background: $color-surface`).\n- **`color-on-primary`** is the colour of a label written on the primary colour: a primary button's text, a selected day, a pressed toggle. The dark primary is light, so its label is dark. `wf theme` prints each pair and its contrast, and `A13` names a pair below the WCAG AA ratio.\n- **`setTheme`** takes `\"light\"`, `\"dark\"` or `\"system\"`, and the choice is kept across visits. With `\"system\"`, the dark theme applies whenever the reader's system prefers dark (`prefers-color-scheme: dark`).\n- **`theme`** reads the choice, and stays current. A `Bool` prop given a condition follows it, so `outlined: theme != \"light\"` outlines every button but the chosen one.")

    }
}
